1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,800
Here is the hot hydrogen iodide tube again,

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:05,120
at about four hundred and fifty degrees, where

3
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,560
K is forty-nine.

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:09,960
But this time nobody let it settle first.

5
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:13,600
Someone has just mixed 0.20 moles per litre

6
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:18,400
of hydrogen, 0.20 of iodine and 0.50

7
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:19,840
of hydrogen iodide.

8
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:23,040
It has not reached equilibrium, so something is

9
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:24,320
about to change.

10
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:27,120
Will the tube make more hydrogen iodide, or

11
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:28,640
break some down?

12
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:30,720
There is a way to know before anything

13
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:31,440
moves.

14
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:35,386
So far K has always taken the settled

15
00:00:35,667 --> 00:00:36,026
values.

16
00:00:36,587 --> 00:00:39,866
Now take the same fraction, hydrogen iodide squared

17
00:00:39,947 --> 00:00:42,666
over hydrogen times iodine, and put in the

18
00:00:42,747 --> 00:00:45,706
concentrations in the tube right now, settled or

19
00:00:45,787 --> 00:00:46,386
not.

20
00:00:46,667 --> 00:00:49,466
That number is the reaction quotient, Q.

21
00:00:49,947 --> 00:00:52,026
It follows the same rules as K, with

22
00:00:52,107 --> 00:00:54,906
powers for coefficients, and solids and the solvent

23
00:00:55,027 --> 00:00:55,546
left out.

24
00:00:56,107 --> 00:00:58,346
At equilibrium Q is K.

25
00:00:58,747 --> 00:01:01,146
At any other moment, Q can be any

26
00:01:01,227 --> 00:01:01,786
value.

27
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,520
Substitute the values now.

28
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:09,720
Hydrogen iodide squared is 0.50 squared, which is

29
00:01:09,960 --> 00:01:11,560
0.25.

30
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:16,600
Underneath, hydrogen times iodine is 0.20 times

31
00:01:16,680 --> 00:01:21,080
0.20, which is 0.040.

32
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:26,200
So Q is 0.25 over 0.040,

33
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:28,280
which is 6.25.

34
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:30,940
Now compare it with K.

35
00:01:31,020 --> 00:01:33,900
Each tick on this line is ten times

36
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,860
the one before, so small and large numbers

37
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:37,500
fit on it.

38
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:42,220
Q is 6.25 and K is forty-nine, so

39
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:44,340
Q is smaller than K.

40
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:47,340
Compared with the reactants, this tube holds less

41
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:49,660
hydrogen iodide than a settled tube at this

42
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:50,780
temperature would.

43
00:01:51,100 --> 00:01:54,300
So which reaction is quicker, hydrogen and iodine

44
00:01:54,380 --> 00:01:57,500
joining, or hydrogen iodide splitting?

45
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:02,060
For a single-step reaction like hydrogen and iodine,

46
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:04,460
the forward rate is a fixed number times

47
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:07,660
hydrogen times iodine, and the reverse rate is

48
00:02:07,860 --> 00:02:11,260
another fixed number times hydrogen iodide squared.

49
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:14,620
At equilibrium the rates are equal, so K

50
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:17,020
is the ratio of those fixed numbers.

51
00:02:17,260 --> 00:02:18,060
Divide the two.

52
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:21,180
The fixed numbers give K, and the concentrations

53
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:23,340
give the Q fraction upside down.

54
00:02:23,820 --> 00:02:27,020
So forward over reverse is K over Q.

55
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:31,820
That is forty-nine over 6.25, about eight, so

56
00:02:31,900 --> 00:02:35,020
the forward reaction runs about eight times faster,

57
00:02:35,100 --> 00:02:37,100
and hydrogen iodide is made.

58
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:41,260
As hydrogen iodide forms, the top of Q

59
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:44,700
grows and the bottom shrinks, so Q climbs.

60
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:48,380
The forward rate falls, the reverse rate rises,

61
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:50,620
just as in the flask videos, until the

62
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:53,180
two are equal, because K over Q is

63
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:53,980
then one.

64
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:58,220
That happens exactly when Q reaches K, here

65
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:03,500
at 0.10, 0.10 and 0.70,

66
00:03:03,580 --> 00:03:06,300
the settled tube from the ICE table video,

67
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:08,460
where Q is forty-nine.

68
00:03:08,540 --> 00:03:10,060
Q chases K.

69
00:03:11,267 --> 00:03:13,106
Now start from the other side.

70
00:03:13,347 --> 00:03:17,806
A tube holds 0.05 of hydrogen, 0.05 of

71
00:03:18,067 --> 00:03:22,506
iodine and 0.80 of hydrogen iodide.

72
00:03:22,787 --> 00:03:25,986
That is almost all hydrogen iodide, so does

73
00:03:26,147 --> 00:03:26,946
nothing more form?

74
00:03:27,347 --> 00:03:28,306
Work out Q.

75
00:03:28,947 --> 00:03:33,586
0.80 squared is 0.64, over 0.05

76
00:03:33,747 --> 00:03:39,906
times 0.05, which is 0.0025,

77
00:03:39,987 --> 00:03:42,706
so Q is 256.

78
00:03:42,867 --> 00:03:44,466
K is forty-nine.

79
00:03:44,547 --> 00:03:45,906
Which way will it run?

80
00:03:45,987 --> 00:03:47,266
Pause here to answer.

81
00:03:57,667 --> 00:04:00,466
Q is above K, so this tube has

82
00:04:00,547 --> 00:04:03,266
too much hydrogen iodide for this temperature, and

83
00:04:03,347 --> 00:04:05,146
the reverse reaction wins.

84
00:04:05,427 --> 00:04:09,986
Forward over reverse is 49 over 256, about

85
00:04:10,147 --> 00:04:13,826
0.19, so the reverse is about five times

86
00:04:13,907 --> 00:04:14,666
faster.

87
00:04:14,947 --> 00:04:18,386
Hydrogen iodide splits, Q falls, and the tube

88
00:04:18,467 --> 00:04:20,666
ends at the same settled tube again.

89
00:04:20,947 --> 00:04:23,986
The first tube was mostly hydrogen iodide too,

90
00:04:24,107 --> 00:04:26,146
yet its Q was below K.

91
00:04:26,387 --> 00:04:28,706
Whether there is too much product depends on

92
00:04:28,787 --> 00:04:31,506
K, so work out Q and compare.

93
00:04:32,734 --> 00:04:35,213
If Q equals K, as in the settled

94
00:04:35,374 --> 00:04:37,933
tube, forward and reverse run at the same

95
00:04:38,014 --> 00:04:40,093
rate and nothing changes overall.

96
00:04:40,574 --> 00:04:44,093
That does not mean equal concentrations: this tube

97
00:04:44,174 --> 00:04:49,533
has 0.10, 0.10 and 0.70.

98
00:04:49,574 --> 00:04:52,253
And if a flask holds only reactants, like

99
00:04:52,294 --> 00:04:53,773
the P C L five flask at the

100
00:04:53,854 --> 00:04:56,893
start, the top of Q is zero, so

101
00:04:57,054 --> 00:04:59,373
Q is below any K and the reaction

102
00:04:59,454 --> 00:05:00,253
runs forward.

103
00:05:00,814 --> 00:05:03,133
If it holds only products, the bottom is

104
00:05:03,214 --> 00:05:06,013
zero, Q is off the scale, above any

105
00:05:06,094 --> 00:05:08,173
K, and it runs in reverse.

106
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:12,160
This also explains the disturbance videos.

107
00:05:12,440 --> 00:05:17,240
Take the settled tube, 0.10, 0.10 and

108
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:21,000
0.70, where Q is forty-nine.

109
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:23,960
Now, in the same sealed tube, add 0.20

110
00:05:24,120 --> 00:05:28,120
moles per litre of hydrogen, so hydrogen is

111
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:30,040
0.30.

112
00:05:30,120 --> 00:05:32,440
The bottom of Q gets bigger, so Q

113
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:37,720
drops to 0.49 over 0.030, about sixteen,

114
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,240
below K.

115
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:42,760
Forward over reverse is forty-nine over sixteen, about

116
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:45,960
three, so the forward reaction wins, uses up

117
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:48,200
some of the extra hydrogen, and the mixture

118
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:49,160
shifts right.

119
00:05:50,367 --> 00:05:53,326
Taking out some hydrogen iodide does the same,

120
00:05:53,447 --> 00:05:56,766
and adding hydrogen iodide pushes Q above K

121
00:05:56,847 --> 00:05:58,286
and sends it left.

122
00:05:58,367 --> 00:06:01,806
K never changed: it is still forty-nine.

123
00:06:02,007 --> 00:06:05,646
Adding or removing a substance changes Q only.

124
00:06:05,807 --> 00:06:08,446
Only a change of temperature changes K, and

125
00:06:08,527 --> 00:06:09,966
that is a later video.

126
00:06:11,167 --> 00:06:12,086
Your turn.

127
00:06:12,367 --> 00:06:15,406
Ammonia is made from nitrogen and hydrogen in

128
00:06:15,487 --> 00:06:18,206
a sealed vessel with an iron catalyst, held

129
00:06:18,287 --> 00:06:21,486
at four hundred degrees Celsius, where K is

130
00:06:21,567 --> 00:06:24,246
0.50 for this equation.

131
00:06:24,607 --> 00:06:26,686
A mixture has just been made up, with

132
00:06:26,767 --> 00:06:30,926
nitrogen at 0.40 moles per litre, hydrogen at

133
00:06:31,007 --> 00:06:35,646
0.50 and ammonia at 0.20.

134
00:06:35,807 --> 00:06:39,006
One: calculate Q for N two plus three

135
00:06:39,247 --> 00:06:42,366
H two making two N H three.

136
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:45,166
Two: will the mixture make more ammonia or

137
00:06:45,247 --> 00:06:46,886
less, and why?

138
00:06:47,167 --> 00:06:48,446
Pause here to answer.

139
00:06:58,867 --> 00:07:02,626
Write Q as ammonia squared over nitrogen times

140
00:07:02,707 --> 00:07:03,826
hydrogen cubed.

141
00:07:04,387 --> 00:07:08,066
Ammonia squared is 0.040.

142
00:07:08,147 --> 00:07:13,186
Hydrogen cubed is 0.50 times 0.50 times

143
00:07:13,267 --> 00:07:18,066
0.50, 0.125, and times the nitrogen

144
00:07:18,227 --> 00:07:21,106
that is 0.050.

145
00:07:21,227 --> 00:07:26,866
So Q is 0.040 over 0.050,

146
00:07:26,947 --> 00:07:29,266
which is 0.80.

147
00:07:29,427 --> 00:07:33,186
Q is above K, 0.50, so the mixture

148
00:07:33,387 --> 00:07:36,066
holds too much ammonia for this temperature.

149
00:07:36,147 --> 00:07:39,106
The reverse reaction is faster and ammonia breaks

150
00:07:39,307 --> 00:07:41,346
down, so it makes less.

151
00:07:41,427 --> 00:07:44,386
If you got 0.20, you left the cube

152
00:07:44,467 --> 00:07:46,866
off the hydrogen, and that wrong number sits

153
00:07:46,947 --> 00:07:49,266
below K, so you would have said more

154
00:07:49,307 --> 00:07:50,386
ammonia.

155
00:07:50,467 --> 00:07:53,426
If you found 0.80 and still said more

156
00:07:53,467 --> 00:07:56,546
ammonia, you flipped the rule: a Q above

157
00:07:56,627 --> 00:07:59,666
K means too much product, not too little.

158
00:08:00,867 --> 00:08:02,626
So when a question gives you a mixture

159
00:08:02,707 --> 00:08:05,346
and a K, write the expression, put in

160
00:08:05,387 --> 00:08:09,026
the concentrations from now, calculate Q, and compare

161
00:08:09,107 --> 00:08:11,026
it with K at the same temperature.

162
00:08:11,587 --> 00:08:14,146
Q below K, the reaction runs forward.

163
00:08:14,627 --> 00:08:16,626
Q above K, it runs back.

164
00:08:17,027 --> 00:08:19,266
Equal, nothing changes overall.

165
00:08:19,747 --> 00:08:22,066
That gives you the direction, not how far

166
00:08:22,147 --> 00:08:22,706
it goes.

167
00:08:23,187 --> 00:08:26,146
Finding how far uses an ICE table and

168
00:08:26,307 --> 00:08:28,946
K, and the harder cases come next.

169
00:08:30,167 --> 00:08:31,606
Here are the key notes.

170
00:08:31,847 --> 00:08:33,766
Pause the video if you need more time

171
00:08:33,847 --> 00:08:34,646
to copy them.
